# AI Notes — environment variables
#
# Scope every one of these to PRODUCTION ONLY in the Vercel dashboard, or
# password-protect preview deployments. A preview URL otherwise runs the same
# code against the same keys, on a hostname nobody is watching.
#
# Confirm the repo is private and .env is gitignored BEFORE creating any key.

# --- Auth ---------------------------------------------------------------
# A passphrase, not four digits. The throttle in api/auth.mjs is per warm
# instance and will not stop a determined guesser.
APP_PASSCODE=

# Signs the session cookie. Not in the original manifest — added because a
# bare boolean cookie can be forged by anyone who can type document.cookie.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Transcription ------------------------------------------------------
SPEECHMATICS_API_KEY=

# Only set this if Speechmatics confirm a different regional endpoint for your
# account. Leave unset to use the default.
# SPEECHMATICS_API_BASE=https://asr.api.speechmatics.com/v2

# --- Extraction ---------------------------------------------------------
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_REGION=eu-west-2

# Confirm the exact id in the Bedrock console for eu-west-2 before first use.
# A leading "eu." means a cross-region inference profile: AWS may serve the
# request from any EU region, not London alone. That changes DPIA §2.7 from
# "UK only" to "UK and EU". A plain id stays in London but depends on on-demand
# capacity being available there. Choose deliberately, then write the choice
# into the DPIA.
BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0
